    date "2021-10-05T02:17:10Z"
    title "Derek Chauvin Still Eligible for $1 Million Pension"
    description "Hundreds of police officers who have been convicted of felonies can still get their pensions.   &#10;Derek Chauvin, who murdered Minneapolis man George Floyd in May 2020, is eligible for his pension totaling $1 million, despite the murder conviction.   &#10;Melanie Hicken, a senior writer and investigative reporter for CNN, joins &#8220;Making the Case&#8221; to discuss officers getting their pensions.  &#10;&#8220;A pension guarantees you a certain set amount of money every year until you pass away,&#8221; Hicken says.     &#10;&#10;All this and more on &#8220;Making the Case.&#8221;  &#10;&#10;To watch BNC programming, visit https://bnc.tv/how-to-watch/   &#10;&#10;Follow BNC on social media:    &#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/BNCNews  &#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/BNCNews   &#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/bncnews/?hl=en  &#10;&#10;#DerekChauvin #Pensions #GeorgeFloyd"
