    description "In the trial of former Brooklyn Center police officer Kim Potter, Daunte Wright&#8217;s autopsy report was shared in court today as an assistant medical examiner said his gunshot wound wasn&#8217;t survivable. &#10;&#10;Also in Minnesota, former police officer Derek Chauvin is reportedly set to change his plea to guilty in the federal civil rights case against him. &#10;&#10;Myles Cosgrove, the detective who fatally shot Breonna Taylor during a raid, is appealing his termination from the Louisville Metro Police Department. &#10;&#10;BNC legal correspondent Laura McNeal joins Marc Lamont Hill on &#8220;Black News Tonight&#8221; to break down these cases. &#10;&#10;All this and more on &#8220;Black News Tonight.&#8221; &#10;&#10;To watch BNC programming, visit https://bnc.tv/how-to-watch/ &#10;Follow BNC on social media: &#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/BNCNews  &#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/BNCNews  &#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/bncnews/?hl=en &#10; &#10;#KimPotter #DerekChauvin #MarcLamontHill"
