  node [
    id 428
    label "SfHKxmlawMA"
    step 0
    date "2022-07-09T19:34:36Z"
    title "DONS CHILDREN"
    description "Don't be surprised by Derek Chauvin's insulting message to George Floyd's children&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;George Floyd changed America. The very fabric of American society was altered in nine minutes and 29 seconds. by the protests that followed and the division it caused among those who believe that black lives matter and those who believe that 'blue&#8221; lives matter instead. Floyd never intended to be a martyr. but sadly. he became one. Some feel that Floyd and his family got justice when Derek Chauvin was sentenced to 22 years for the murder of Floyd &#8211; after all. when cops commit acts of violence against people of color. they are almost never held accountable Take a look at the police officers who killed Breonna Taylor But as Chauvin was given a 20 year federal sentence this week for violating Floyd's civil rights &#8212; a sentence that will run alongside his 22 year state conviction for on duty murder &#8212; he didn't t not excused. And even if part of America feigns shock at this lack of apology. I'm not surprised. Why would Chauvin be sorry? He clarified his thoughts the second he filed an appeal to overturn his murder conviction. What about this action that indicates remorse? Chauvin wished Floyd's children seemingly flippant 'good luck' as he was transferred to a federal prison this week after being convicted of the federal crime (he will now likely swap solitary confinement to a US prison). state versus a lower security. more comfortable federal facility). But he got the best of them and refuses to apologize for it. And his 22 years in prison will not bring their father back; it won't get them a Father's Day next to Floyd instead of next to his headstone. Insultingly. Chauvin added that he hopes Floyd's children 'have some great advice on becoming great adults' before he is taken away. A culture of violence. especially violence against black people. proliferates in American police academies. Michigan police were recently forced to apologize and conduct a review after discovering they were using images of black men for target practice; elsewhere. officers were caught mocking Elijah McClain's death as if it were a joke; and New York cops have been heavily criticized for selling fundraising coins with the image of a black man hunted on them. Even the Minneapolis police   the police working where Chauvin was previously employed   were found to have 'engaged in a pattern of racism' in their policing. How many examples of concerning and racist rhetoric in American policing have yet to come to light or may never come to light? An individual did not kill George Floyd; systemic racism in policing did. Black people are killed by police at disproportionate rates. are more likely to be subject to traffic stops and searches. and are more likely to face more serious charges or longer sentences for the same charges than their white counterparts. Racism runs through the veins of police. so much so that the 'Black Lives Matter' declaration. alongside demands to examine how police treat black people. was enough to spur this 'blue lives matter' counter movement. '. But. as many cops and cop supporters don't realize. there is no blue life. A cop can take off his uniform if he feels it makes him a target of violence. but black people can't take our skins off. As a nation we have let down George Floyd. Eric Garner. Breonna Taylor. Tamir Rice and so many other black people who have been killed at the hands of the police expecting change to come from the systems that harm us . How can we expect justice from the American justice system when it has been proven that judges give harsher sentences to people with darker skin? Even in juvenile cases. black boys are more likely to be charged as adults than their white peers. Why would Chauvin apologize when every institution. from arresting to sentencing. is so slowly crushing black lives? While Chauvin's knee may no longer be on Floyd's neck. the knee of a culture that views us as threats remains on the neck of every black person in America. And we still can't breathe when those...&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;#news"
    channeltitle "Not&#237;cias em V&#237;deo"
    channelid "UCxkwKWtSGPR0OP1h7hLU_nw"
